## Terms and Conditions

### Definitions

- "Plotypus" refers to the 2D and 3D graphing calculator software, including all source code, assets, documentation, and any implementation thereof.
- "Software Implementation" refers to any implementation of Plotypus or its substantive components in a programming language.
- "Hardware Implementation" refers to any embodiment of Plotypus or its substantive components in hardware, including but not limited to FPGA bitstreams, ASIC tape-outs, custom silicon, microcontroller firmware, and any photolithographic or non-reprogrammable integrated circuit.
- "Substantive Component" refers to any non-trivial portion of Plotypus that constitutes a recognisable subsystem (e.g. the input parser, the evaluator, the rendering pipeline, the chrome/compositing layer).
- "Sale" refers to any transaction in which Plotypus or any Substantive Component thereof is the principal good or service being exchanged for monetary or equivalent compensation, including paid downloads, paid app-store distribution, paid hosted access, and paid licensing of the software or hardware embodiment itself.
- "Licensee" refers to any individual or entity using Plotypus.

